# Architecture rules

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE-GUIDELINES.md` for full detail.

## Boundaries

- **`projects/background/`**: Gemini fetch, storage, tab messages — **no DOM**
- **`projects/content-script/`**: bridge only — **no DOM mutation**
- **`projects/dom-updater/`**: MAIN world DOM + postMessage — **no `chrome.*`**
- **Popup/options**: extension UI + scripting — **no page storage of secrets**

## Data & secrets

- API key: `chrome.storage.local.geminiApiKey` — background + options only
- HTML sent to Google — document privacy impact when changing capture/preprocessing
- Do not widen `extension/manifest.template.json` permissions without explicit user request and doc update

## Messaging

- Changing a message `type` or payload shape requires updating **all** producers/consumers (grep repo) + `libs/messaging`
- Keep `event.source === window` checks on postMessage listeners

## Injection order

- Popup analyze: inject `content-script/main.js` (default world) **then** `dom-updater/main.js` with `world: 'MAIN'`

## Build

- Ship **`dist/pdp-ai/`** after `npm run build:extension`; do not load unpacked from repo root
